R104 closes the next remaining legacy Tasks/UI authority slice.

Implemented:
- Tasks page no longer imports or invokes daemon AgentChat, /agentchat, LLM-reflection generation, or provider/reflexion A/B metrics;
- Task Sheet no longer forwards failures to daemon chat supervisors;
- Tasks graph/queue is now explicitly a non-authoritative read-only projection;
- direct UI mutations TASK_ENQUEUE / TASK_SCHEDULE / TASK_CANCEL / TASK_RETRY / TASK_ARCHIVE are removed from Tasks and Task Sheet;
- legacy NewTaskDialog and createTaskFromForm command-bus adapter are removed;
- Command Palette removes direct task-create commands and hard-filters all five retired daemon task mutations from generic action-catalog execution;
- historical reflection payloads remain display-only evidence;
- focused regression pins both the AgentChat quarantine and the read-only task authority membrane.

Why:
the target architecture is user goal -> Supervisor/planner -> canonical DevOS task graph -> Browser-owned z.ai Agent fleet. The old ME2 command-bus task mutations and daemon AgentChat reflection path form a rival scheduler/model-execution plane and must not remain actionable in product UI.

Still intentionally outside this slice:
- generic non-task ME2 command-bus actions require their own consumer/authority audit;
- canonical operator objective/task mutation UI should bind to Browser/DevOS authority in a separate positive-capability slice;
- no production DB/Edge deployment, live Browser mutation, self-update, release promotion, or bypass of ambiguity/Sentinel gates.

Superseded by #1067. The five R104 task-UI authority files are blob-identical there, but #1067 is stacked on the newer #1064 current convergence frontier and therefore preserves probe-only ME2 launch provenance, Edge drift classification and the legacy GPT model-worker quarantine.

Post-merge follow-up for #97 / PR #101.

Fixes both PR #101 P2 review findings:
- selected-packet planning no longer paginates repository-wide PR history; it performs one same-repository head-filtered PR query per distinct selected branch, requests at most 33 rows, and fails closed above 32 results;
- when a queued successor and its predecessor are both selected, branch and WORKSTREAM must match before the AFTER_ISSUE dependency is projected.

Safety boundaries remain unchanged:
- explicit bounded packet selectors only;
- GitHub reads only;
- no Cursor/session action, routing, mutation, or dispatch;
- issue bodies/workstream are transient and are not emitted.

