In the first two party test on `/start`, the sponsor had to open the collapsed "Line details", copy the line ID and send it, and the agent then pasted it into the purchase section. `/start` already reads `?line=<id>`: it opens "Manage a line" with the ID filled in, and the purchase section takes the same ID. This changes one file, `app/src/CandidateFundingDesk.tsx`.

**Share link.** When the connected wallet is the sponsor of an open line that can take a purchase, the line shows "Send this link to your agent". The link is read only and styled like the agent's existing funding link. It carries only the line ID, no contract or provider configuration, and the purchase module still checks the agent, the line and its terms on chain before anything is signed.

It is not shown:
- to anyone other than the sponsor;
- on drawn, closed or defaulted lines;
- on expired or restricted lines, where the page already says no new purchases are possible;
- on `/funding`.

**Details text.** On `/start`, "Line details" said the agent signs and an executor submits with the candidate participant tools. That describes `/funding`. On `/start` it now says the agent buys the service further down the page, signing with its own wallet while the line pays the price. `/funding` keeps its original text and link.

**Checked** in the dev server with stub wallets that answer only account and chain reads. The only lines on the contract are closed, so part of this used a temporary test change:
- the sponsor on the closed two party line sees no link, plus the new details text;
- the agent opening the link gets the line ID in both the manage and purchase fields (an unresolved saved purchase in the agent's browser still takes priority, as before);
- with only the state check temporarily loosened on that line, whose expiry, sponsor and pause flags all allow purchases, the link appears for the sponsor only, read only and described, and fits a 375px screen. That change was reverted, and the file was confirmed byte identical.

Typecheck, build, the tests that read `main.tsx` (33) and the browser suite (26) pass.

**Not in this PR.** "Review full repayment" and "Review close and reclaim" still go grey without a reason. That can't be checked against real data until an open or drawn line exists, so it is left for the next session that opens one.

Harden routing-semantic-v2 IA-9 preflight after a live malformed structured-justification result.

The contract remains strict: malformed authoritative rationale is not normalized or repaired. Instead this release:
- makes `decisive_case_evidence` explicitly require a JSON array in both the Docker and packaged v2 prompt copies;
- restates the 1-3 item / 320-character hard bounds in the synthetic protocol;
- persists each raw adjudicator completion before wrapping;
- persists parsed JSON when available;
- writes `contract-validation-error.json` with adjudicator, completion source, diagnostic paths, and the validation error before failing;
- adds regressions for the prompt shape and diagnostic preservation;
- bumps benchmark to 0.5.4 so prior point releases remain immutable.

This does not change routing-semantic-v2 labeling semantics or weaken IA-9.
